-- title:
--   Tate cardinalities of the archimedean ideles of a cyclic extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$, so that the Galois group is cyclic generated by $\sigma$. Let $D$ be a Galois descent datum for the adeles of $L$ over $K$: a monoid homomorphism $\tau \mapsto D.\mathrm{act}\,\tau$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathrm{AdeleRing}\,(\mathcal{O}_L)\,L$, compatible with the structure map from $L$ in the sense that $D.\mathrm{act}\,\tau$ carries the image of $x \in L$ to the image of $\tau x$, and with each $D.\mathrm{act}\,\tau$ continuous. Let $\Phi$ be a multiplicative automorphism of the unit group $(\mathbb{A}_{L,\infty})^\times$ of the infinite adele ring of $L$, assumed to compute the archimedean component of the $\sigma$-action: for every unit $x$, the first component of $D.\mathrm{act}\,\sigma$ applied to the pair $(x, 1)$, with $1$ the unit of the finite adele ring of $L$, equals $\Phi(x)$ (nothing is required of the finite component). On the additivisation $\mathrm{Additive}\,(\mathbb{A}_{L,\infty})^\times$, let $d$ and $N$ be additive endomorphisms pinned on generators by $d(u) = \Phi(u) - u$ and $N(u) = \sum_{i=0}^{n-1} \Phi^i(u)$, where $n = \#\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$. Finally let $s_i(v) = \#\{w \in \mathrm{InfinitePlace}\,L : w|_K = v\}$ for each infinite place $v$ of $K$. Then the quotient of $\ker d$ by the intersection of the range of $N$ with $\ker d$ has cardinality $\prod_{v} n / s_i(v)$, the product being over all infinite places of $K$ and the divisions being natural-number divisions, and the quotient of $\ker N$ by the intersection of the range of $d$ with $\ker N$ has cardinality $1$.
--
--   This is the archimedean contribution to the Herbrand-quotient computation for a cyclic extension of number fields: the two cardinalities are the orders of the Tate cohomology groups $\hat H^0$ and $\hat H^1$ of the cyclic group $\langle\sigma\rangle$ acting on the units of the infinite adele ring, computed here through the explicit derivation and norm endomorphisms $d$ and $N$. It is used in the idele-class-group side of the Herbrand quotient identity, feeding [`M4aHerbrand.ideleClass_herbrandQuotient_eq_finrank`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.ideleClass_herbrandQuotient_eq_finrank), [`M4aHerbrand.ideleClassGroup_tateCard_zero_ne_zero_and_finrank_dvd`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.ideleClassGroup_tateCard_zero_ne_zero_and_finrank_dvd) and [`M4aHerbrand.exists_adeleBaseChange_normCoset_index_ne_zero_and_finrank_dvd`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_adeleBaseChange_normCoset_index_ne_zero_and_finrank_dvd).
